   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2012-09-06T18:26:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Error when fitting multivariate probit",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On 9/6/12 1:53 PM, Bob Carpenter wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On 9/6/12 12:49 PM, William Morris wrote:\r<br>\r<br>&gt;&gt;    parameters {\r<br>&gt;&gt;      vector[J] Z[n];\r<br>&gt;&gt;      real B[J, K];\r<br>&gt;&gt;      cov_matrix[J] S;\r<br>&gt;&gt;    }\r<br>&gt;&gt;    model {\r<br>&gt;&gt;      matrix[n, J] Mu;\r<br>&gt;&gt;      real p[n, J];\r<br>&gt;&gt;      for (j in 1:J) {\r<br>&gt;&gt;        B[j] ~ normal(0, 100);\r<br>&gt;&gt;      }\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; This can be vectorized to B ~ normal(0,100);\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Sorry -- didn&#39;t read this closely enough.\r<br>We can&#39;t yet take whole matrices for B in\r<br>\r<br>   B ~ normal(0,100);\r<br>\r<br>so the way you do it is the most efficient way\r<br>to do this.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "nzFn13_3A6QJ",
