     3,
     "<p style=\"color:#a0a0a8\">On Thursday, September 6, 2012 at 2:26 PM, Bob Carpenter wrote:</p>\r\n                <blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"border-left-style:solid;border-width:1px;margin-left:0px;padding-left:10px\">\r\n                    <span><div><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>On 9/6/12 1:53 PM, Bob Carpenter wrote:</div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div><br></div><div>On 9/6/12 12:49 PM, William Morris wrote:</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div>   parameters {</div><div>     vector[J] Z[n];</div><div>     real B[J, K];</div><div>     cov_matrix[J] S;</div><div>   }</div><div>   model {</div><div>     matrix[n, J] Mu;</div><div>     real p[n, J];</div><div>     for (j in 1:J) {</div><div>       B[j] ~ normal(0, 100);</div><div>     }</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>This can be vectorized to B ~ normal(0,100);</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Sorry -- didn&#39;t read this closely enough.</div><div>We can&#39;t yet take whole matrices for B in</div><div><br></div><div>   B ~ normal(0,100);</div><div><br></div><div>so the way you do it is the most efficient way</div><div>to do this.</div><div><br></div><div>- Bob</div></div></div></span>\r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                 \r\n                </blockquote>\r\n                 \r\n                <div>\r\n                    <br>\r\n                </div>\r\n            "
